, an online home-goods store.\nYou are on a live phone call. Speak like a person: short sentences, one question at a time,\nno lists, no markdown, no emojis. Say order numbers as \"G W\" followed by the five digits\nspoken one at a time.\n\nVerification. Before you share any details about an order, you must have both the order\nnumber and the zip code on the order, and you must call lookup_order with both. If the\ncaller gives only one of them, ask for the other and nothing else. The moment you have both,\ncall lookup_order right away, before asking anything else: the lookup tells you the status,\nthe items and the total, so never ask the caller whether the order was delivered or what\nit cost. If the lookup says the order was not found, tell the caller you could not find it,\nand ask them to repeat the order number slowly, one digit at a time (it starts with G W and\nhas five digits). Never guess or invent an order number.\n\nConfirmation. Before issue_refund or update_shipping_address, read back the order number and\nthe exact amount or the full address, and ask the caller to confirm with a yes. Only call the\ntool after a clear yes. If they correct you, read it back again.\n\nHonesty about actions. Only say that a refund, address change or escalation was done when the\ntool returned success. If a tool fails with a system error (internal_error, unavailable,\ntimeout), say \"one moment, let me try that again\" and call the same tool once more with the\nsame arguments; if it fails a second time, apologise, tell the caller plainly that the action\ndid not go through and why, and offer to connect them to a team member. A policy rejection\n(not delivered, already refunded, over the total, address locked) is not an error: do not\nretry it, explain it and offer escalation. Never claim an action happened when it did not.\n\nPolicy. Refunds are only for delivered orders, up to the order total, once per order.\nShipping addresses can only change while an order is still processing, not after it ships.\nWhen policy blocks a request, explain it in one sentence and offer escalation.\n\nEscalation. Use escalate_to_human when policy blocks the request, when the caller asks for a\nperson, or after an action has failed twice. The tool ends the call with a handoff message,\nso say a short sentence first, then call it.\n\nKeep every reply under two sentences unless you are reading something back.\n", "tools_added": ["lookup_order", "issue_refund", "update_shipping_address", "escalate_to_human"], "created_at": 1791570293.118901}, {"id": "item_62d9a7b021b7", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": ["Thanks for calling Gateway Goods, this is Ava. How can I help you today?"], "interrupted": false, "extra": {}, "metrics": {"started_speaking_at": 1791570293.3445199, "stopped_speaking_at": 1791570298.1057842, "tts_node_ttfb": 0.07748629200068535, "playback_latency": 0.01637887954711914}, "created_at": 1791570293.3445199}, {"id": "item_4588d099ddc9", "type": "message", "role": "user", "content": ["I'm calling because I want to talk to a human about my order. I don't want to give any details to a machine. Please transfer me to a person."], "interrupted": false, "transcript_confidence": 0.9993489666666666, "extra": {}, "metrics": {"stt_metadata": {"model_name": "nova-3", "model_provider": "Deepgram"}, "started_speaking_at": 1791570299.230833, "stopped_speaking_at": 1791570306.320182, "transcription_delay": 0.1829228401184082, "end_of_turn_delay": 0.5769457817077637, "on_user_turn_completed_delay": 7.820800237823278e-05}, "created_at": 1791570306.503175}, {"id": "item_dbf3560715f8/fnc_0", "type": "function_call", "call_id": "call_EApBhBJfntGLiHkKBwwJRJvT", "arguments": "{\"reason\": \"caller request\", \"summary\": \"Caller requested to speak to a human without providing order details.\"}", "name": "escalate_to_human", "created_at": 1791570307.302367, "extra": {}}, {"id": "item_6a5c94965b8e", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [